With the exception of Devin Leary, a sixth-round compensation pick to the Baltimore Ravens, all of the signal-callers saw improvement from their first season to when they entered the college game. Exactly what an NFL team wants with a young guy entering the program.
Improvement year to year, especially for players on the younger side, is extremely unknown. It is hard to predict what a player as important as a quarterback is going to do in his sophomore, junior, and senior seasons based just off of one year. It is more difficult now than ever before with the transfer portal as a major player.
It is far from linear. Truly, the only thing that ultimately matters from the start to the end of one’s college football career is that you are in a better spot than where you left it. In most cases, that is exactly what happens.
